Lets the simulated host's commit guard pass a symlink whose kind matches
what the engine expected, whatever its target, as before d12fec3 (§7.5 step
6), so a retarget between a losing version's record and the commit that
displaces it goes through. Only that fix's target comparison is undone: the
guard still compares a file's exec bit, SetMeta is still guarded, and the
scan fast path is unchanged.

test: delocal-sim regressions::a_retarget_under_a_pending_commit_is_changed_underneath_in_another_run

diff --git a/crates/sim/src/sim.rs b/crates/sim/src/sim.rs
index 4e18586..53335d7 100644
--- a/crates/sim/src/sim.rs
+++ b/crates/sim/src/sim.rs
@@ -2731,7 +2731,10 @@ fn rel(s: &str) -> RelPath {
 fn expected_matches(file: Option<&File>, expected: Option<&Observed>) -> bool {
     match (file, expected) {
         (None, None) => true,
-        (Some(f), Some(e)) => e.unchanged_by_stat(&f.observed()),
+        (Some(f), Some(e)) => e.unchanged_by_stat(&Observed {
+            hash: e.hash,
+            ..f.observed()
+        }),
         _ => false,
     }
 }
